/// The build's version, printed by `lll --version` and shown in the board's
/// rail footer, so the browser says which build is serving it.
///
/// A literal, bumped with [project] version in lisette.toml when tagging. The
/// gate asserts the two agree, so a missed bump fails before a release does.
///
/// This used to run `git describe --tags` at startup, which answered with
/// whatever repository the caller was standing in. lll is run inside other
/// people's projects, so it usually was one: in a checkout tagged v9.9.9 the
/// binary reported "lll 9.9.9", and outside any repo it fell back to a
/// hardcoded literal that a release could forget to bump. v0.3.0 shipped
/// reporting 0.2.0 that way (LLL-431).
pub fn version() -> string {
  "0.3.2"
}
